---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **차트에 오르는 한국 시리즈는 몇 곳에서 나오나.** (`/who-makes-it`)
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **줄세우지 않는다.** 「어느 회사가 1등인가」를 안 낸다. 몇 곳이면 절반인가만 낸다.
 *    이름은 등급 없이 **알파벳순**으로만 싣는다.
 * ⛔ **영화는 안 센다.** 회사가 붙은 것이 37.7% 뿐이라 반쯤 빈 자료로 쏠림을 재면
 *    빠진 회사가 「작은 회사」로 보인다. 뺀 까닭을 지면이 말한다.
 * ⛔ 「방송사는 원래 많이 걸린다」는 반론을 **표 안에** 넣는다 — 역할별로 따로 낸다.
 * ⛔ 시장 쪽 수와 **단위가 다르다.** 견줌으로만 놓고 같다고 말하지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-who-makes-it.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-who-makes-it.json';

const 어느것 = data.roles[0];
const 제작 = data.roles[1];
const TITLE = 'How many companies make the Korean series that chart?';
const DESC =
  `Of ${어느것.firms} companies credited on the ${어느것.series} Korean series that reached a Netflix `
  + `country top 10, ${어느것.halfTakesFirms} account for half of them. Counting production companies `
  + `only, it is ${제작.halfTakesFirms} of ${제작.firms}.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/who-makes-it">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    We already measure how few titles fill half of a country’s Korean chart. This is the same ruler
    pointed the other way: how few companies fill half of what charts.
  </p>
  <p class="q">{data.question}</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Half of it comes from {어느것.halfTakesFirms} companies</h2>
    <p class="note lead-in"><b>How this is counted.</b> {data.unit}</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Credit counted</th><th>Companies</th><th>Series they cover</th>
            <th>Companies for half</th><th>Those companies, alphabetically</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.roles.map((r) => (
            <tr class={r.key === 'production' ? 'edge' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{r.label}</td>
              <td>{r.firms}</td>
              <td>{r.series} <span class="fine">({r.seriesCoveragePc}%)</span></td>
              <td class="tot">{r.halfTakesFirms}</td>
              <td class="nm">{r.namesInHalf.join(', ')}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>The names are in alphabetical order, not in size order.</b> This page does not rank companies
      and the table cannot be read as a league. It answers one question — how few it takes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The objection: broadcasters cover a lot by definition</h2>
    <p class="warn">
      A network airs everything it airs, so counting first-broadcaster credits will always look
      concentrated — {data.roles[2].firms} broadcasters cover {data.roles[2].series} series between
      them. That is why the row to read is <b>{제작.label}</b>: counting only companies Wikidata lists
      as having <i>made</i> the series, <b>{제작.halfTakesFirms} of {제작.firms}</b> still account for half.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      ⚠ That row rests on a thinner base — production credits are attached to {제작.series} series,
      {' '}{제작.seriesCoveragePc}% of the {data.seriesTotal} that charted. It is the most meaningful
      cut and the least complete one, and both of those are true at once.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Most companies here have one series</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Series credited to the company</th><th>Companies</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.firmSizeBands.map((b) => (
            <tr><td class="nm">{b.band}</td><td class="tot">{b.firms}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The long tail is real: {data.firmSizeBands[0].firms} of {어느것.firms} companies appear on exactly
      one charting series. Concentration at the top and a crowd at the bottom are the same fact seen
      from two ends.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why films are not in this table</h2>
    <p class="warn">{data.whySeriesOnly}</p>
    <p class="note">
      Films are {data.filmsTotal} of the titles we hold and only {data.filmsWithFirm} carry a company
      at all — <b>{data.filmCoveragePc}%</b>, against {어느것.seriesCoveragePc}% for series. Fixing
      that needs a source Wikidata does not have.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Beside the market figure — not the same unit</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Across {data.marketCount} markets, the median country fills half its Korean chart places with
      {' '}{data.marketHalfTakesMedian} titles; the United States needs {data.marketHalfTakesUS} and
      Vietnam {data.marketHalfTakesVN}.
      {' '}<b>⚠ Those count titles and this page counts companies</b>, so the two numbers are not
      comparable and we are not comparing them. They are placed side by side because both ends of the
      same pipe turn out to be narrow.
      {' '}<a href="/catalogue-depth">The market side →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/who-makes-it" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from, and what they cannot answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Wikidata and Netflix</b> — {data.source}</li>
      <li>
        <b>A credit is not a share of the work.</b> Wikidata records that a company is attached, not
        how much of the budget or the decision it held.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Corporate groups are not merged.</b> Companies inside one group are listed separately
        because we did not confirm the ownership tree, and guessing it would change the answer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Only titles that charted are here.</b> A company whose series never reached a top 10 is
        absent, so this is not a census of Korean production.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/catalogue-depth">All markets side by side</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/where-it-moved">Where Korean titles gained and lost</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
